.Dd November 8, 2026
.Dt DMA_FENCE_CHAIN_GET_PAYLOAD_STATUS 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dma_fence_chain_get_payload_status
.Nd get the status of a fence-chain point and its nested payload
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In linux/dma-fence-chain.h
.Ft int
.Fn dma_fence_chain_get_payload_status "struct dma_fence *fence"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn dma_fence_chain_get_payload_status
reads the status of one selected fence, including nested chain payloads.
The caller must hold a reference to the non-NULL
.Fa fence
and must not hold a fence lock.
The function borrows the reference and does not consume it.
The outer reference keeps each immutable chain payload alive.
.Pp
A pending fence returns zero, even when an error has already been set.
A completed fence with an error returns that error.
A successfully completed chain is unwrapped and its payload is checked.
A successfully completed non-chain fence returns one.
The first completed error from outer to inner takes precedence.
.Pp
Previous timeline points still gate completion but do not supply the selected
point's error.
Completed previous points may already have been collected.
Other fence types, including arrays, retain their own status semantics.
The function does not flatten them or change any fence's error field.
The payload walk is iterative; underlying signaling probes are unchanged.
.Pp
This function is a native DRM compatibility extension.
It does not change the behavior of
.Fn dma_fence_get_status .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The function returns zero for pending work, one for success, or a negative
error code for completed work that failed.
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Fn dma_fence_chain_get_payload_status
function first appeared in EmberBSD.
